## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
Severity: MEDIUM  
AMAT’s revenue heavily depends on semiconductor capital expenditure, which is cyclical. Its customer concentration in foundries (e.g., TSMC, Samsung) exposes it to capex cycles. While the company benefits from secular AI-driven demand, near-term risks include inventory digestion and potential market saturation in consumer electronics.  

